                <pb facs="0714" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.512/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé at Tangier</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Rand</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-19T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1923—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>19. Your July 16, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>Inform Spanish Agency at Tangier as well as American citizens and protégés that
                    neither Department nor your agency will be able to support refusal of latter to
                    pay consumption tax from date of release of Cohen’s shipment, provided they are
                    not meanwhile subjected to this tax.</p>
                <p>Advise interested colleagues. Spanish Embassy here informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
